e  he told us a little bit more about the  story as well and in this interview he  said so you have his very specific gifts  his intelligence his treachery his  mischief his magic and then seeing him  go up against more formidable opponents  the likes of which he has never seen or  known so in the interview Tom Hiddleston  says that in the Loki series were going  to see him go up against more formidable  opponents the likes of which he has  never seen before and this is extremely  interesting because if we think about it  we have seen him go up against some  really powerful villains he went up  against hella in thor ragnarok who even  his brother thor couldn't kill and of  course he went up against Thanos and  Avengers infinity war whom ended up  killing him or at least that remains to  be seen  but we do know that this alternate  timeline version of Loki is eventually  going to make his way back into the main  MCU timeline we know that the Loki  series is going to directly set up some  of the events that take place in Thor  for love and thunder including Loki  jumping back to the main MCU timeline  and bringing with him a version of Mele  near this is supposedly how Jane Foster  gets Millner and transforms into Jane  Foster Thor and this is rather  interesting as well because Mueller  typically has a worthiness enchantment  on it so unless Loki visited an  alternate reality in which Mueller did  not have a worthiness enchantment on it  Loki is now worthy enough to pick up  Mueller so we are going to see just a  total transformation from Loki in this  series because again the 2012 Loki that  escapes with the tesseract is a  completely different Loki than we see in  the beginning of infinity war so we're  definitely going to see Loki do a major  transformation over the course of this  series and then it has been officially  confirmed that Loki is going to tie in  to Doctor Strange in the multiverse of  madness and this was confirmed just a  few days ago by Disney CEO